<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n49673" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἰά̄λεμ-ος</span></b> , 
			Ion.
		
		<b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἰήλ-</span></b> , ὁ, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>lament, dirge</i>,
			used by Trag. in lyr., <i><span class="en">
				A.
				<u>Supp.</u>
				115
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				E.
				<u>Rh.</u>
				895
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				<u>Tr.</u>
				1304
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				<u>Ph.</u>
				1033
			</span></i>, etc.; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τὸν ἰ. ἀρίστευσε</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Theoc.
					15.98
				</span></i>
			: rare in Prose, <i><span class="en">
				Metrod.
				<u>Herc.</u>
				831.17
			</span></i> (s.v.l.)&lt;*&gt;  prov., <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἰαλέμου ψυχρότερος</span>, of something
			tedious and dull, <i><span class="en">
				Zen.
				4.39
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>II.</b> as
			Adj., <i>melancholy</i>, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">γόοι</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					E.
					<u>HF</u>
					109
				</span></i>
			(lyr., s.v.l.); but usu., </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>2.</b>
			<i>tedious, dull, stupid</i>, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ποιηταί</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Luc.
					<u>Pseudol.</u>
					24
				</span></i>
			; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἰατροί</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Gal.
					14.617
				</span></i>
			: as Subst., <i>dullard, oaf</i>, <i><span class="en">
				Men.
				236
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Hermog.
				<u>Id.</u>
				2.6
			</span></i>; title of play by <i><span class="en">
				Amphis
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Ath.
				2.69b
			</span></i>. (Perh. from the cry <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἰή</span>.)</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
